 "_about": "Warehouse 126 (the owner, 2026-11-22): a library of font pairs, so a page never gets a font the model invented and never Heebo everywhere. Per supported script (scripts.json) four pairs, each a display face for headings and a body face, both from Google Fonts (OFL; rights_sources.json 'google_fonts'), each with the weights the page loads -- the design contract's two weights, 400 and 700, or 400 alone for a display face that has one weight. Every family and weight was checked against fonts.googleapis.com/css2 on 2026-11-22 for its script's subset (Hebrew pairs serve the 'hebrew' subset, Arabic pairs the 'arabic' one); tests/test_font_pairs_load.py loads every pair in Chromium. 'tones' are the section library's art directions (directions.json): a business's category gives its palette, the palette its direction, and the direction the two pairs it may get; the business itself picks one of them (omni_prod/typography.pair_for). Formal and elegant pages get a serif display face (Frank Ruhl Libre, David Libre; Amiri, El Messiri; Playfair Display, Fraunces); warm and bold pages a friendly or heavy one (Secular One, Rubik; Lalezar, Noto Kufi Arabic; Space Grotesk, Archivo). No family belongs to two scripts, so a Hebrew page and an Arabic page never share a font.",
